{"name":"Scarlet","hex":"#ff2400","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Scarlet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from English, a modern variant of Scarlett, or from the common noun scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Scarlet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scarlet (cloth)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarlet was a type of fine and expensive woollen cloth common in Medieval Europe. In the assessment of John Munro, 'the medieval scarlet was therefore a very high-priced, luxury, woollen broadcloth, invariably woven from the finest English wools, and always dyed with the red dye kermes, even if mixed with woad, and other dyestuffs. There is no evidence for the use of the term scarlet for any other textile, even though other textiles, especially silks, were also dyed with kermes.'"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Petrarch-ranks-of-man-remediis-milan-braidense-ad-xiii-30-f1-c1400.jpg/330px-Petrarch-ranks-of-man-remediis-milan-braidense-ad-xiii-30-f1-c1400.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_(cloth)","wikidata":"Q1220957"},{"title":"Scarlet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarlet is a bright red color, sometimes with a slightly orange tinge. In the spectrum of visible light, and on the traditional color wheel, it is one-quarter of the way between red and orange, slightly less orange than vermilion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/RCMP-female-officer.jpg/330px-RCMP-female-officer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_(color)","wikidata":"Q2268159"},{"title":"Scarlet (Doja Cat album)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarlet is the fourth studio album by American rapper and singer Doja Cat. It was released through Kemosabe and RCA Records on September 22, 2023. Disillusioned with pop music and dissatisfied with music critics questioning her status as a rapper, Doja Cat felt inspired to create a \"masculine\" follow-up to her third studio album, Planet Her (2021). Her first project with no features since her debut extended play, Purrr! (2014), the record marks a departure from the pop-driven sounds of its predecessor, being predominantly centered around rapping."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0b/Doja_Cat_-_Scarlet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_(Doja_Cat_album)","wikidata":"Q117769123"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Weltliche_Schatzkammer_Wienc.jpg/500px-Weltliche_Schatzkammer_Wienc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Weltliche_Schatzkammer_Wienc.jpg/500px-Weltliche_Schatzkammer_Wienc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Coronation Mantle of Roger II of Sicily, silk dyed with kermes and embroidered with gold thread and pearls. This kind of cloth seems to have been denoted by the Arabic siklāt. Royal Workshop, Palermo, Sicily, 1133–34. Kunsthistorisches Museum, Vienna.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWeltliche_Schatzkammer_Wienc.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Nelson_Tower_in_Scarlet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5188743.jpg/500px-Nelson_Tower_in_Scarlet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5188743.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Nelson_Tower_in_Scarlet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5188743.jpg/500px-Nelson_Tower_in_Scarlet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5188743.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANelson_Tower_in_Scarlet_-_geograph.org.uk_